SECTION 3: CLEAN-ROOM ARCHITECTURE & ZERO-DEPENDENCY RUNTIME
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
lh-jsonl-logger is engineered from first principles as an independent, clean-room
telemetry logging engine, cryptographic hash-chain verifier, and audit posture
evaluator.

It operates with 100% zero external Composer runtime dependencies, requiring only
native PHP 8.2+ core extensions:
  - ext-hash (SHA-256 and HMAC-SHA256 hash-chaining routines)
  - ext-json (Strict canonical JSON serialization and parsing)
  - ext-spl (Standard PHP Library data structures and exceptions)
  - Standard POSIX filesystem and stream locking primitives (flock, chmod)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 4: TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS & STANDARDS CONFORMANCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This software conforms to the following international and industry standards:
  - RFC 8259: The JavaScript Object Notation (JSON) Data Interchange Format
  - JSON Lines (NDJSON / JSONL): Newline-delimited JSON streaming format
  - NIST FIPS 180-4: Secure Hash Standard (SHA-256)
  - RFC 2104: HMAC: Keyed-Hashing for Message Authentication
  - OASIS SARIF v2.1.0: Static Analysis Results Interchange Format
  - CERT-In Cyber Security Directions: 180-day log retention compliance (CWE-778)
  - OWASP Top 10 / CWE: CWE-117 (Log Injection), CWE-532 (PII in Logs),
    CWE-353 (Missing Integrity Check), CWE-276 (Permissive File Permissions),
    CWE-362 (Race Condition / Atomic Locking), CWE-400 (Uncontrolled Resource Consumption)
